  { number := 152, text := "### 4.2 Binary format (`.sstt`)" },
  { number := 153, text := "" },
  { number := 154, text := "A Tech Tree file SHALL use the extension `.sstt`. The payload SHALL be, in this order:" },
  { number := 155, text := "" },
  { number := 156, text := "1. Magic: twelve ASCII bytes `SSTECHTREE01` and no zero byte in those twelve bytes." },
  { number := 157, text := "2. A `CompactSize` count of nodes." },
  { number := 158, text := "3. That many node records. Each node record SHALL include a `CompactSize` node identity, a `CompactSize` node kind (Clause 3.5), a `CompactSize` byte length of the path, and that many path bytes as UTF-8 that is also pure ASCII in this repository." },
  { number := 159, text := "4. A `CompactSize` count of directed edges." },
  { number := 160, text := "5. That many edge records. Each edge record SHALL include a `CompactSize` source node identity, a `CompactSize` destination node identity, and a `CompactSize` edge kind (Clause 3.5)." },
  { number := 161, text := "" },
  { number := 162, text := "A writer of `.sstt` files exists in this Lake package (`lean/Sstt.lean`). Authors MUST NOT claim a Surmount product writer is shipped." },
  { number := 163, text := "" },
  { number := 164, text := "### 4.3 `CompactSize`" },
  { number := 165, text := "" },
  { number := 166, text := "Lengths and counts in a `.sstt` file SHALL use Bitcoin canonical `CompactSize`." },
  { number := 167, text := "" },
  { number := 168, text := "1. For a value `n` less than 253, the encoding is one byte whose value is `n` (markers `0x00` through `0xfc`)." },
  { number := 169, text := "2. For a value `n` at least 253 and less than 65536, the encoding is marker `0xfd` followed by two payload bytes in least significant byte first order holding `n`." },
  { number := 170, text := "3. For a value `n` at least 65536 and less than 4294967296, the encoding is marker `0xfe` followed by four payload bytes in least significant byte first order holding `n`." },
  { number := 171, text := "4. For a value `n` at least 4294967296, the encoding is marker `0xff` followed by eight payload bytes in least significant byte first order holding `n`." },
  { number := 172, text := "5. The encoding MUST be the shortest form that can hold the value. A decoder MUST reject a longer form of a value that fits a shorter form." },
  { number := 173, text := "" },
  { number := 174, text := "Golden vectors that a companion encoding and test SHALL match (same bytes as `btc-verified`):" },
  { number := 175, text := "" },
  { number := 176, text := "1. `0` encodes as the single byte `0x00`." },
  { number := 177, text := "2. `252` encodes as the single byte `0xfc`." },
  { number := 178, text := "3. `253` encodes as `0xfd 0xfd 0x00`." },
  { number := 179, text := "4. `65535` encodes as `0xfd 0xff 0xff`." },
  { number := 180, text := "5. `65536` encodes as `0xfe 0x00 0x00 0x01 0x00`." },
  { number := 181, text := "" },
  { number := 182, text := "A decoder MUST reject the non shortest form `0xfd 0xfc 0x00`." },
  { number := 183, text := "" },
  { number := 184, text := "This Lake package SHALL restate those laws as spec encodings and SHALL prove encode then decode for the golden values and for values less than 253 that this package can prove without `mathlib`. Full `UInt64` theorems `decode_encode`, `decode_canonical`, and `encode_length_le` remain in `btc-verified`. This repository pins that tree as Form 1 at `ref/btc-verified`. This Lake package does not vendor those theorems." },
  { number := 185, text := "" },
  { number := 186, text := "### 4.4 Encoded graph MUST be a graph with no directed cycle" },
  { number := 187, text := "" },
  { number := 188, text := "1. The encoded graph (Clause 3.2) MUST be a graph with no directed cycle: there SHALL be no directed cycle in the edge relation used as the tree." },
  { number := 189, text := "2. If a producer would emit a cycle, that output does not conform." },
  { number := 190, text := "3. The markdown citation graph (Clause 3.3) MAY contain directed cycles. Those cycles do not by themselves make this specification fail. A producer (when one exists) SHALL choose an orientation with no directed cycle or drop edges so the encoded graph has no directed cycle." },
  { number := 191, text := "4. Companion Lean SHALL encode a cycle check on finite graphs of natural number identities and SHALL prove small fixtures: the empty graph has no directed cycle, a chain has no directed cycle, and a two node loop has a directed cycle." },
  { number := 192, text := "5. This slice does not require `repo_links_check` to fail the whole repository when numbered specifications cite each other in both directions." },
  { number := 193, text := "" },
  { number := 194, text := "### 4.5 Markdown path links in this repository" },
  { number := 195, text := "" },
  { number := 196, text := "1. Markdown links that reference material present in this repository (relative links, paths under `ref/`, sibling `.lean` files, numbered specifications, and similar path targets) SHALL resolve to a path that exists." },
  { number := 197, text := "2. That rule is also Clause 11.4 of `0000_spec.md`. Authors of numbered specifications SHALL follow it." },
  { number := 198, text := "3. The Lean program `repo_links_check` SHALL scan numbered `NNNN_*.md` files at the repository root, and SHALL scan `README.md`, for markdown links of the form `[text](target)`." },
  { number := 199, text := "4. That program SHALL skip targets that begin with `http://` or `https://`." },
