  { number := 248, text := "" },
  { number := 249, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unimplemented requirement, or an out of scope item named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
  { number := 250, text := "" },
  { number := 251, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
  { number := 252, text := "" },
  { number := 253, text := "1. fargo has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for fargo. This document does not invent a number for fargo. This document does not steal 0005, 0006, 0007, 0008, 0009, 0010, or 0011 for fargo." },
  { number := 254, text := "2. SSSP has no assigned specification number. This document does not create a numbered file for SSSP. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating SSSP." },
  { number := 255, text := "3. The Carbonado Network Protocol has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Number 0005 is CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is RSI (`0006_RSI.md`), not Carbonado. Number 0007 is Continuous Integration (`0007_CI.md`). Number 0008 is Formal Vibefication (`0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). Number 0009 is Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) (`0009_PDOSS.md`). Unlicense remains the license. Number 0010 is Surmount Systems (`0010_Surmount_Systems.md`). Number 0011 is this specification. This document does not create a file for Carbonado." },
  { number := 256, text := "4. Lean Machine is specified in `0013_Lean_Machine.md`. That document is specification 0013. Legal Lean and Holy Lean remain named components without separate numbered specifications." },
  { number := 257, text := "5. Number 0009 was briefly Vocabulary, then Unlicense, and is now Public Domain Open Source Software (PDOSS) by operator order. Unlicense remains the license. The word catalog lives in CATE (`0005_CATE.md`). This document does not assign 0009 to fargo or to Carbonado. A numbered Vocabulary file MUST NOT exist. The form checker MUST fail if that file is present." },
  { number := 258, text := "6. Number 0012 is Majestic `Memex` (`0012_Majestic_Memex.md`) and is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that product is ready for use." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "### 6.2 Format and proof that are not shipped as product" },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "1. This document specifies the `.sstt` format. This Lake package includes a Lean writer and reader of `.sstt` files (`lean/Sstt.lean`, command `sstt_write`). That writer is not a shipped memex product. Number 0012 is specified. The command at `~/majestic` is still a proof of concept. Work on the writer and on CompactSize in this Lake package is not finished. Treating that Lake writer as a shipped Surmount product is Cons False in the Tech Tree proofs module. Wiring a producer into a product tree stays leftover." },
  { number := 263, text := "2. Bitcoin `CompactSize` is specified and proved for `UInt64` in `btc-verified` (`BtcVerified.CompactSize`, theorems `decode_encode`, `decode_canonical`, `encode_length_le`). The Form 1 pin is `ref/btc-verified`. This specifications repository does not vendor that tree into this Lake package. This Lake package restates the markers, least significant byte first payload, and shortest form, and proves golden vectors and small encode then decodes without `mathlib`. Full `UInt64` coverage remains residual to `btc-verified`. Copying those full `UInt64` theorems into this Lake package is Cons False in that same module. Full `UInt64` CompactSize theorems stay in `ref/btc-verified`. This Lake package MUST NOT copy those theorems." },
  { number := 264, text := "3. The encoded graph MUST be a graph with no directed cycle. Markdown citation among numbered specifications MAY cycle. `repo_links_check` in this slice checks that path targets exist. It does not fail the repository because `0000_spec.md` and `0005_CATE.md` cite each other. A producer, when one exists, still MUST emit an encoded graph with no directed cycle." },
  { number := 265, text := "4. `repo_links_check` does not parse every HTML `href`. The floor is markdown `[text](target)` links. Reference style links are residual." },
  { number := 266, text := "" },
  { number := 267, text := "### 6.3 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 268, text := "" },
  { number := 269, text := "1. The products named here are ongoing and are not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that those products never started or do not exist." },
  { number := 270, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product as specified in `0007_CI.md` and in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 6.3. This document does not claim that match already holds." },
  { number := 271, text := "3. `lean/TechTreeSpec.lean` encodes selected claims. `lean/TechTreeProofs.lean` proves those claims. `0011_Surmount_Systems_Tech_Tree.lean` encodes the physical lines of this markdown file. `lean/Proofs_0011.lean` proves identities of that line encoding. Those modules are not a proof that a `.sstt` producer exists. They are not a proof that beastdb, SSSSS, Slake, or Continuous Integration are ready for use. Mixing those encodings with their proofs in one mash is Cons False in the Tech Tree proofs module. Those modules are not a proof that a producer is wired into a product tree." },
  { number := 272, text := "" },
